  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "N.Venugopal vs State Of Kerala on 20 May, 2019 Author: V Raja Vijayaraghavan Bench: V Raja Vijayaraghavan In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Raja Vijayaraghavan V Monday, The 20Th Day Of May 2019 / 30Th Vaisakha, 1941 Crl.MC.No. 1800 of 2015 S.T.No.1599/2004 of Chief Judl.Magistrate, Ernakulam Petitioner/Accused No.6: N.Venugopal, Aged 52 Years, Partner, M/S.Hong Kong Restaurant, M.G.Road, Kochi-682035. Residing At 43/566A, Citizen Road, Semetry Junction, Kochi-682018. By Advs. Sri.Zakeer Hussain Sri.V.Tekchand Respondents/Complainant & State: 1 State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam, Kochi-682031. 2 The Food Inspector Corporation Of Kochi, Ernakulam-682011. By Advs. Sri.E.D.George,Sc,Cochin Corporation Sri.E.D.Georgesccochin Corporation N.Venugopal vs State Of Kerala on 20 May, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/2925832/ 1 Smt M K Pushpalatha Sr Pp This Criminal Misc. Case Having Been Finally Heard On 20.05.2019,",
    "facts": "The petitioner herein is the 6 th accused in S.T.No.1599 of 2004 on the file of the Chief Judicial Magistrate, Ernakulam. The said proceeding was based on a complaint lodged by the Food Inspector arraying as many as 9 persons alleging commission of offence punishable under Sections 2(ia)(a),(m), 7(i) and 7(v) r/w. Section 16(i)(a)(i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and Appendix B item No.A.11.01.11 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1957. 2. According to the prosecution, the 1st accused is the vendor, 2nd accused is the licensee and accused Nos.3 to 6 are the partners of the 7th accused, the firm. The accused No.8 and 9 are the persons from whom the vendor had purchased toned milk.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the proceedings against the accused Nos.3, 4 and 5 were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court by Annexure-A2 order dated 14.9.2012. This was based on the premise that there were no pleading in the complainant that the partners were in charge and responsible for the day to day conduct of the firm. The petitioner has also been arrayed in his capacity as the partner of the firm and hence the proceedings against him are also liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] is the submission. 6. In Paragraph No.3 of Annexure-A2, this Court, while quashing the proceedings against accused Nos. 2 to 5, had occasion to observe as follows: \"3. The factual foundation of pleading that petitioners were in charge of the business of the firm is conspicuously absent in the complaint.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the proceedings against the accused Nos.3, 4 and 5 were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court by Annexure-A2 order dated 14.9.2012. This was based on the premise that there were no pleading in the complainant that the partners were in charge and responsible for the day to day conduct of the firm. The petitioner has also been arrayed in his capacity as the partner of the firm and hence the proceedings against him are also liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK] is the submission.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "6. In Paragraph No.3 of Annexure-A2, this Court, while quashing the proceedings against accused Nos. 2 to 5, had occasion to observe as follows: \"3. The factual foundation of pleading that petitioners were in charge of the business of the firm is conspicuously absent in the complaint."
  },
